<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Luang Phrabang</h1><p class="st-meta">1707 CE – 1947 CE · capital Luang Prabang</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northern successor of Lan Xang, whose royal house survived Siamese and French overlordship to become the monarchy of modern Laos.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>During the succession conflicts after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sourigna-vongsa">Sourigna Vongsa's</a> death, his grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingkitsarath">Kingkitsarath</a>, with backing from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xishuangbanna">Sipsongpanna</a>, established himself at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a> in 1707 as king, separate from the court of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Kingdom of Vientiane</a>. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/lan-xang">Lan Xang</a> was thereby formally divided.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom ruled the northern Lao highlands, with Lao, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmu-people">Khmu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hmong-people">Hmong</a> subjects, and was frequently threatened by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/myanmar">Burma</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a> and Siam. From 1779 it was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of Siam. Its capital, with temples such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wat-xieng-thong">Wat Xieng Thong</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phra-bang">Phra Bang</a> image, was the religious heart of Lao kingship.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haw-wars">Chinese Haw</a> raiders sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Prabang</a> in 1887, the French consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auguste-pavie">Auguste Pavie</a> rescued King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oun-kham">Oun Kham</a>, and the kingdom came under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-protectorate-of-laos">French protectorate of Laos</a> in 1893. Its king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisavang-vong">Sisavang Vong</a> became monarch of the unified <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-laos">Kingdom of Laos</a> in 1946 to 1947.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Luang Phrabang" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Luang_Phrabang_(1707-1893).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1707 CE – 1947 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Luang Prabang</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kingkitsarath, Oun Kham, Sisavang Vong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lao</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/laos">Laos</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Luang Prabang, Luang Prabang</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1827&amp;focus=kingdom-of-luang-phrabang" aria-label="Kingdom of Luang Phrabang on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7436 1441 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Luang Phrabang lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7756 1697L7756 1697M7756 1697L7576 1622M7756 1697L7753 1923M7756 1697L7754 1922M7756 1697L7784 1767M7756 1697L7784 1767"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7756 1697h0M7576 1622h0M7753 1923h0M7754 1922h0M7784 1767h0M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7756 1697h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7756 1697h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Luang Prabang. <a href="/atlas?year=1827&amp;focus=kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
